[Music]  well that is taps  and it is some of the most heartfelt  memorial day tributes that contain no  words just those 24 notes taps the  unmistakable bugle call played at  military funerals and this memorial day  weekend cbs news on the road  correspondent steve hartman is back with  something he's very passionate about  it's called taps across america steve  joins us live from catskill new york to  talk about what's becoming a tradition  for you and for viewers good morning  steve so good to see you this morning  good morning sherry thanks for having me  you bet so for people who may not know  or heard of taps across america  tell us a little about it and what are  you asking people to do this year  we're asking buglers and trumpet players  really any kind of musician  to play taps  at three o'clock local time  and they don't have to go far just out  on the front porch or the backyard patio  we just want as many people as possible  commemorating the holiday  with taps  why is it important that we pause at 3  p.m local time to play taps what is it  about that time  well three o'clock is the national  moment of remembrance  and i think it's important that we pause  and um i'm asking people to play taps  because i kind of felt like  the purpose of the holiday had gotten  lost to some extent there were picnics  and  hamburgers and hot dogs and water  balloon fights but really the whole  reason we celebrate is to honor our  fallen and i thought this would be the  perfect way to put out the call  literally to pause for just these 24  notes and remember why we have memorial  day in the first place  so you're getting your responses have  been tremendous this is the third year  tens of thousands of people have  participated  all over the country with all kinds of  different instruments what is your  ultimate goal for taps across america  ultimately if this tradition continues  as i dearly hope it does  i like that i would like that no matter  where you live in america from the  biggest cities to the  the furthest out country roads that you  hear taps that it's lofting over every  neighborhood and every street in america  that's my ultimate goal and judging by  the response we've gotten so far and it  builds every year i think we're going to  get there  and you don't have to be a professional  musician right you're just asking  everybody you've even had people learn  how to play an instrument just so they  could participate  we've had lots of people do that and  those are the most emotional videos for  me when people send in their videos  because  you know yeah they're not perfect but i  just think of the hours they spend it's  not that easy to learn but people have  spent hours and they try to play it as  best they can because it means that much  to them and and that's that's what  really gets to me more than anything  okay  we'll have the information of where  people can submit their videos so that  they can participate and i'm sure you'll  pick the best ones and as many as you  can and play them so that people can see  themselves so thank you so much taps  across america we wish you the best  again and i expect that you're going to  get a resounding response like you have  for the last couple of years steve so  thanks so much and we always enjoy  everything you do so and good memorial  day weekend to you  thank you thank you very much for having  me i appreciate it you bet nice to talk  to you as always

